{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["The heh <b>her purifying.</b> The nun is hidden, and it would have been proper to show the heh, as in \"and he called her Noah.\" The meaning of \"the blood of her purifying\" — it is blood of purity, as opposed to the blood of menstruation, and it does not defile. HaShem decreed concerning the male according to the number of the male, whose form is completed in the womb, and the female double. And this is clear and tested." "<b>she shall touch no hallowed thing.</b> Such as tithe and terumah and the flesh of peace-offerings." "<b>nor come into the sanctuary.</b> Into the court of the Tent of Meeting, or into the azarah in the Temple." "<b>the blood of her purifying.</b> Or \"upon the blood of her purifying\" — it is one."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:42.842777887Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}